menu "Core2 DOOM"

config DOOM_QEMU
    bool "Build for Espressif QEMU instead of the Core2"
    default n
    help
        Replaces the M5Unified hardware layer with one that draws to QEMU's
        virtual RGB panel, stubs audio, and plays a scripted input sequence
        that starts a game and exercises the controls. It prints
        "SHOT <name>" on the console when a frame worth capturing is on
        screen; tools/qemu_run.py turns those into screenshots.

endmenu
